            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "So why not check if the dbus path still exists?\n\nWhat is the point of the stash file if we're never using it now?  If there is some case we need to handle, this seems like a pervasive problem in all of the scripts that do these stash files."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Eldin Lee",
                        "email": "eldin.lee@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "eldin-lee"
                    },
                    "message": "These handlers are based on the implementation in change-id If008c241cc0fffd8262bd6c88eaae35215b740ba.\n\n> So why not check if the dbus path still exists?\n\nThese handlers are only used for gpiomon events. The signal has to flip for gpiomon to catch the event, so there\u2019s no case where it gets fired twice without an edge. That\u2019s why I think this check isn\u2019t needed.\n\n\n> What is the point of the stash file if we're never using it now?  If there is some case we need to handle, this seems like a pervasive problem in all of the scripts that do these stash files.\n\n\nThe stash is still used by log-resolve to mark the previous failure event as resolved after the signal flip.\n\nIf other scripts use the same stash logic and someone clears the logs manually, they should hit the same issue too. Then the failure and recovered logs won\u2019t match."
                }
            ],
